# Public Event Registration E2E Harness (Playwright) -- Slice 1.
#
# Separate from .env.local / .env.example on purpose: this harness seeds
# real rows via the Supabase service-role key and drives a real browser, so
# its config must never silently inherit whatever the running app happens
# to be pointed at. Copy this file to .env.e2e.local, fill in real values,
# and load it into your shell before running `npm run test:e2e`
# (e.g. `set -a; source .env.e2e.local; set +a` on macOS/Linux/Git Bash, or
# `Get-Content .env.e2e.local | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '^([^#=]+)=(.*)$') { Set-Item "Env:$($Matches[1])" $Matches[2] } }`
# in PowerShell).
#
# See e2e/README.md for the full setup/run instructions.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the Playwright browser navigates. REQUIRED, no default.
# Built in as always-safe: localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1] -- see
# src/lib/e2e/guards.ts. Everything else, INCLUDING any *.vercel.app
# deployment URL, is rejected by default: Vercel assigns a *.vercel.app
# address to every deployment, production included, so there is no way to
# tell a preview deployment from production by hostname shape alone. The
# harness hard-blocks the known DanceFlow production domains (idanceflow.com,
# www.idanceflow.com) even if you add them to E2E_ALLOW_HOSTS below.
E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: comma-separated extra hostnames to allow beyond the built-in
# localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] allowlist. Use this to run against one specific,
# already-verified-non-production Vercel preview deployment -- add its exact
# hostname (e.g. danceflow-app-git-my-branch-dance-flow.vercel.app), not a
# wildcard. Never add a production hostname here -- it will still be
# rejected by the hard block regardless.
# E2E_ALLOW_HOSTS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase instance the fixture helpers seed data into directly
# (service-role key, bypasses RLS by design -- this is a server-side test
# harness, not the app itself). REQUIRED, no default, no fallback to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
#
# The values below are the standard Supabase CLI local-dev demo keys --
# identical across every `supabase start` installation, published in
# Supabase's own docs, safe to commit, and only usable against a local
# instance (they carry no meaningful secret and are rejected by any real
# Supabase project). If you're running the local Docker Supabase staging
# instance already used elsewhere in this project (container
# supabase_kong_danceflow-local-staging, exposed on 127.0.0.1:54321), these
# work as-is.
E2E_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
E2E_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6InNlcnZpY2Vfcm9sZSIsImV4cCI6MTk4MzgxMjk5Nn0.EGIM96RAZx35lJzdJsyH-qQwv8Hdp7fsn3W0YpN81IU
